WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.339
Sacrifice is a part of any journey.

00:00:06.048 --> 00:00:09.968
Taking on these great challenges
against great odds...

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.764
...that's what makes us human.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:22.564
- "For All Mankind" is an
alternate history of the space race.

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:26.485
- When we come back in to Season 2,
it's almost 10 years later.

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:30.239
It's 1983.
Both sides expand on their moon bases,

00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:32.824
and the competition between
the two superpowers

00:00:32.908 --> 00:00:34.826
has also gotten much more intense.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:39.540
- We're coming in
to an alternate history of the new 1980s.

00:00:39.623 --> 00:00:41.708
The social change is more rapid,

00:00:41.792 --> 00:00:44.378
the development
of technology goes much quicker.

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:46.380
- (alarm chirps)
- No more gas stations.

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:48.632
I got 60 miles on a single charge.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.676
- We have electric cars,
we have cell phones.

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:53.303
Because the Russians
land on the Moon first,

00:00:53.387 --> 00:00:54.888
NASA is not defunded,

00:00:54.972 --> 00:00:58.684
and it pushes us further into technology
in a competitive way.

00:00:59.268 --> 00:01:02.521
- This is Jamestown Actual.
Enjoy the show, everyone.

00:01:03.689 --> 00:01:06.650
- In space,
Jamestown has expanded drastically.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:09.820
There's up to 30 astronauts
on the Moon at any given time.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:13.407
It's a really exciting
leap forward in Season 2.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:17.244
- Let me state as plainly as I can.

00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:20.163
The greatest threat
the United States faces

00:01:20.247 --> 00:01:22.416
is posed by the Soviet Union.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.378
- There's rising tensions
between the superpowers.

00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:29.131
The Cold War, rather than cooling off,

00:01:29.214 --> 00:01:30.257
it's the exact opposite.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.887
- It becomes about
ownership of the Moon

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:37.973
by militarizing the Moon
to try and stake a claim.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:42.311
- The President wants us
to confront the Soviets on the Moon.

00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:45.147
- They're going to need weapons, right?

00:01:45.856 --> 00:01:48.358
- We see the military presence

00:01:48.442 --> 00:01:50.027
and how that affects
life on the Moon.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:53.030
- We need to send a message
to the Soviets.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:54.823
- But there's
gotta be another way.

00:01:56.825 --> 00:01:58.160
- I recommend go to DEFCON 3.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:04.458
- Season 2 is everything you loved
about Season 1

00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:05.751
taken a step further.

00:02:06.001 --> 00:02:08.212
- Bringing the Cold War conflict
to the Moon

00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:11.340
is a big part of Season 2.
It will be quite a shock and surprise.

00:02:11.423 --> 00:02:13.425
- Follow emergency power protocols,

00:02:13.509 --> 00:02:15.260
-scram the nuclear reactors.
- Copy.

00:02:15.928 --> 00:02:19.473
- It's just an exquisitely
executed show

00:02:19.556 --> 00:02:22.601
about human beings
in extreme situations.

00:02:25.187 --> 00:02:27.022
- Once we do this thing...

00:02:28.649 --> 00:02:30.651
...there's no going back.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.571
- PRESIDENT REAGAN: History has asked
much of the Americans of our time.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:39.493
Much more we must
be prepared to give.

